From 89f7cbdbb2e81edac973364a4b43473eb4394224 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:52:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 685/687] test(gpu-model-runner): the stand-in runners carry what
 the runner now reads

Base: candidate-38's patch head 753354cf4 (tree 37b34b8f), the series of
experiments/2026-10-26-spark-ds41f-candidate/candidate-38/vllm/series.

Rationale: six tests build GPUModelRunner stand-ins (GPUModelRunner.__new__ or
a SimpleNamespace) that lacked attributes the series gave the code under test,
and failed at the first read. Each gets what the real runner holds:

- postprocess_sampled trims sampled rows to num_draft_steps + 1 (copy drafts'
  wide verification, e8c696282): test_boundary_capture_uses_recovered_accepted_
  state sets num_draft_steps = num_speculative_steps = 3, one bonus token and
  three drafts, so its four sampled columns are kept whole.
- initialize_kv_cache reads copy_drafter (planned confidences for the adaptive
  verification manager, e8c696282): test_qsa_circular_group_uses_custom_slot_
  mapping sets None.
- initialize_kv_cache computes the block-table geometry through
  _block_table_max_model_len, _block_table_width and _group_cp_size on itself
  (e57a0d844): test_initialize_kv_cache_does_not_dcp_shard_mamba_block_table
  binds the runner's methods to its SimpleNamespace.
- execute_model reads uniform_decode_query_len (the uniform-decode dispatch,
  e8c696282) and, after a logits-only restore, the DP sync's skip_drafts
  (7d3263647) and num_draft_steps for the spec tokens to schedule:
  test_boundary_logits_only_dispatches_pending_cache_tasks sets 1, a sync that
  does not skip drafts, and 0.
- _profile_deepseek_v4_attention binds one block per KV cache group besides the
  null block, from get_kv_cache_groups(self.vllm_config, self.get_kv_cache_spec()):
  test_deepseek_v4_attention_profile_uses_reachable_prefill_and_cleans_up gives
  the runner a config and a spec, patches get_kv_cache_groups to return two
  groups, checks it was asked with them, and expects num_blocks=3 (it expected
  1, the single block the profile bound before).
- sample_tokens reads sink (the sink sampler, 2d832d876):
  test_pipeline_drafts_do_not_depend_on_boundary_checkpoints sets None.

Quality: no runtime change; a test-only patch.

Tests: tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_model_runner_v2.py in spark-ds41f:candidate-38
on dgx4 (GB10): 40 passed (was 20 passed, 20 failed).

Upstream status: the file is Local Inference Lab's (LIL); the fixes follow the
series' own changes to the runner and are not for upstream.
